  "reason": "Core retired a project's execution worker as soon as the project had no open chat or queued/running work, so every routed request on a quiet project (rename, archive, delete, first chat after a pause) paid a worker cold start and the next one paid it again. Workers now stay until a bounded grace (5 min, NEBULA_IDLE_WORKER_GRACE_SECONDS 0..3600) after the project's last accepted command, and the grace ends at once while another project that still wants a worker has a failed admission waiting to retry (#1030's _admission_retry). Selected: Work batch and admission tests (new grace test, override bounds test, updated edit/delete admission test), quiescence and automatic recovery suites, and product help discovery (new test) because docs/CLI.md and docs/MEMORY_BUDGETS.md describe the grace.",
